CHANCERY — PHASE 10 (VDR upload → deal-creation proposal)
Structural sprint · HELD for manual review (first aggregate cross-document AI capability)

=========================================================================
TASK 1 — DISCOVERY (reported, not assumed)
=========================================================================
1(a) REAL deals table schema (docs/schema_snapshot.sql, refreshed this sprint):
     deals(id, org_id, name NOT NULL, slug UNIQUE, description,
           deal_status enum DEFAULT 'draft',
           asset_super_class / asset_class / asset_sub_category  <- TEXT taxonomy KEYS
           sponsor_entity_id, sponsor_name_override,
           target_raise / minimum_investment / expected_return_pct  <- NUMERIC,
           term_months INT, deal_date / close_date DATE, location,
           highlights[] / tags[], is_featured, deal_stage TEXT, + bitemporal cols).
     Only `name` is required. proposed_fields (jsonb) is shaped to this real schema.
     Taxonomy columns are KEYS the AI cannot know -> left null; the AI's free-text
     read goes to proposed_fields.asset_class_hint for the human reviewer to map.

1(b) REAL createDeal mechanism: POST /api/v1/deals ->
     routers.marketplace.create_deal (require_permission 'manage_deals' +
     validate_taxonomy_fields + unique slug + insert + audit_log).
     REUSE (not a parallel path): the deterministic slug->insert->audit core was
     extracted into services.deal_creation.insert_deal; BOTH the marketplace
     endpoint AND VDR approval now call that one function.

1(c) No pre-existing aggregate cross-document AI pattern anywhere. Every prior AI
     call is per-document (document_classifier: "a single document";
     chancery_intake loops one AI call per file). services.vdr_analysis is the
     FIRST call that concatenates extracted_text across a whole document_drop and
     reasons over the batch -- genuinely new capability shape.

=========================================================================
BUILT
=========================================================================
services/vdr_analysis.py   aggregate a drop's extracted_text -> call_claude_json
                           (task_type='vdr_analysis') -> proposed_fields matching
                           the real deals schema -> insert vdr_deal_proposals
                           (status='pending'). Honest confidence gate: refuses to
                           propose from weak signal (needs is_coherent_deal +
                           confidence>=medium + a name + >=2 substantive fields).
                           approve_proposal / reject_proposal review helpers.
services/deal_creation.py  shared insert_deal core (extracted from marketplace).
routers/vdr.py             GET /vdr-proposals . POST /vdr-proposals/{id}/approve
                           . POST /vdr-proposals/{id}/reject .
                           POST /document-drops/{id}/analyze-vdr. approve reuses
                           deal_creation.insert_deal, records created_deal_id, and
                           links EVERY drop doc via document_record_links
                           (record_type='deal', Phase-9 mechanism). manage_deals
                           gated. Registered in main.py.
routers/documents.py       intake gains an `is_vdr` Form flag -- reuses the SAME
                           drop path; when set, runs analyze_drop after the drop
                           completes (best-effort; never fails the upload).
routers/marketplace.py     create_deal now calls the shared insert_deal core.
web (Task 4)               app/admin/vdr-proposals + VDRProposalsManager.jsx
                           (upload form with the is_vdr checkbox + pending-proposal
                           list with approve/decline) and Next proxy routes
                           (/api/documents multipart, /api/vdr-proposals[/id/*]).
DB                         added FK vdr_deal_proposals.created_deal_id -> deals(id)
                           (warranted: deals.id is a stable unique PK). RLS policy
                           on vdr_deal_proposals confirmed correct (NULLIF org GUC).
                           schema snapshot regenerated.

Task 4 reuse decision: there was NO existing Chancery upload UI to bolt the flag
onto (intake had been backend/verify-only; entity/SPV uploaders are different
subsystems), and Phase 5's proposal-review UI was never built as a page either.
So one minimal admin surface was added that reuses the existing intake endpoint
(just adds the checkbox) rather than a separate VDR upload screen.

